1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,270
Forty-nine thousand, nine hundred
and ninety dollars drive-away.

2
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:06,270
For a 320-kilowatt plug-in hybrid SUV,

3
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:11,130
with all-wheel drive and 137
kilometres of electric range.

4
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:16,050
That's the price of the new 2027
GWM Haval H7 plug-in hybrid,

5
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:20,530
which officially launches in
Australia on the 2nd of November 2026.

6
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:22,390
And it's aimed squarely at one car:

7
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:25,870
the Toyota RAV4 one of the
best-selling cars in the country,

8
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:30,310
and, in July 2026, the best-selling
plug-in hybrid in Australia.

9
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:36,550
The cheapest RAV4 plug-in hybrid you
can buy right now starts at $58,840

10
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:38,910
and that's before on-road costs.

11
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:39,870
So on paper,

12
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:42,930
GWM has just undercut Toyota
by thousands of dollars,

13
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:45,470
with more power and more electric range.

14
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:46,970
But is it really that simple?

15
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:50,090
In this video, I'll compare
the two properly price,

16
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:51,850
power, range, towing,

17
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:55,130
warranty and resale and tell you what
the numbers on the brochure don't.

18
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:59,350
Because the cheapest car on the day
isn't always the cheapest car to own.

19
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:03,910
And with Toyota bringing a cheaper
RAV4 plug-in hybrid in early 2027,

20
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:06,040
the fight is only just getting started.

21
00:01:06,668 --> 00:01:09,718
First, a bit of context about who GWM is.

22
00:01:09,768 --> 00:01:14,238
Great Wall Motors GWM has been selling
cars in Australia for eighteen years,

23
00:01:14,288 --> 00:01:18,738
and in October 2026 it was celebrating
that anniversary with price cuts across

24
00:01:18,788 --> 00:01:19,838
its range.

25
00:01:19,888 --> 00:01:23,538
Its Haval Jolion small SUV has become
one of the best-selling cars in

26
00:01:23,588 --> 00:01:25,438
Australia in 2026.

27
00:01:25,488 --> 00:01:27,058
And like most Chinese brands,

28
00:01:27,108 --> 00:01:30,638
it's been growing fast while some
long-established brands go backwards.

29
00:01:30,688 --> 00:01:33,138
You can see that shift in
the official sales numbers.

30
00:01:33,188 --> 00:01:36,318
In September 2026, according to VFACTS,

31
00:01:36,368 --> 00:01:40,518
Geely sales were up 870 per cent
on the same month a year earlier,

32
00:01:40,568 --> 00:01:43,758
Omoda Jaecoo was up 344 per cent,

33
00:01:43,808 --> 00:01:48,038
Leapmotor 106 per cent
and BYD 61 per cent.

34
00:01:48,088 --> 00:01:51,278
Toyota, by comparison,
was down 3.5 per cent.

35
00:01:51,328 --> 00:01:55,058
Toyota is still the biggest brand
in the country by a long way but the

36
00:01:55,108 --> 00:01:57,518
pressure is coming from every direction.

37
00:01:57,568 --> 00:01:59,338
First, let's meet the challenger.

38
00:01:59,388 --> 00:02:04,758
The new GWM Haval H7 is a
boxy, five-seat mid-size SUV.

39
00:02:04,808 --> 00:02:08,558
It's actually the second H7 GWM
has sold here in a short time.

40
00:02:08,608 --> 00:02:12,558
CarExpert reported that the outgoing
model was replaced after "a little over a

41
00:02:12,608 --> 00:02:16,058
year" on sale and to the end of July 2026,

42
00:02:16,108 --> 00:02:20,498
GWM had delivered only 636 of the old H7s,

43
00:02:20,548 --> 00:02:24,518
compared with 8,759 of its Haval H6.

44
00:02:24,568 --> 00:02:26,558
So the new one has a lot to prove.

45
00:02:26,608 --> 00:02:28,418
It's also bigger than you might expect.

46
00:02:28,468 --> 00:02:34,858
CarExpert lists the five-seater
at 4,680 millimetres long 4,800

47
00:02:34,908 --> 00:02:40,158
including the spare wheel carrier on
the tailgate and 1,950 millimetres wide,

48
00:02:40,208 --> 00:02:43,358
with a 2,738-millimetre wheelbase.

49
00:02:43,408 --> 00:02:45,958
That boxy shape is a
big part of its appeal.

50
00:02:46,008 --> 00:02:49,658
It looks more like a rugged
off-roader than a typical family SUV.

51
00:02:49,708 --> 00:02:52,858
It comes in two powertrains, both
with all-wheel drive as standard.

52
00:02:52,908 --> 00:02:57,258
The hybrid uses a 1.5-litre turbo
petrol engine with electric motors,

53
00:02:57,308 --> 00:03:01,458
for 182 kilowatts and 670 newton-metres,

54
00:03:01,508 --> 00:03:05,338
with claimed fuel use of 7.0
litres per hundred kilometres.

55
00:03:05,388 --> 00:03:09,558
The plug-in hybrid uses the same
1.5-litre turbo petrol engine,

56
00:03:09,608 --> 00:03:12,998
but with a much bigger
33.7-kilowatt-hour battery.

57
00:03:13,048 --> 00:03:17,978
Combined output is a huge 320
kilowatts and 670 newton-metres.

58
00:03:18,028 --> 00:03:23,158
GWM claims 0 to 100 kilometres
an hour in 4.9 seconds,

59
00:03:23,208 --> 00:03:26,518
an electric-only range of 137 kilometres,

60
00:03:26,568 --> 00:03:33,858
and a combined range of 844
kilometres on the Chinese WLTC test.

61
00:03:33,908 --> 00:03:36,678
And GWM says interest has been strong.

62
00:03:36,728 --> 00:03:41,758
It reported around 1,500 expressions
of interest after the H7's debut at the

63
00:03:41,808 --> 00:03:44,118
Everything Electric show in September.

64
00:03:44,168 --> 00:03:46,058
GWM Australia's head of marketing,

65
00:03:46,108 --> 00:03:50,868
Steve Maciver, said: "We have high
expectations for the all-new Haval H7."

66
00:03:52,464 --> 00:03:52,239
Now the prices.

67
00:03:52,289 --> 00:03:55,109
According to CarExpert and Cars24,

68
00:03:55,159 --> 00:03:57,949
these are the H7 drive-away
prices at launch.

69
00:03:57,999 --> 00:04:00,496
The H7 Lux hybrid:

70
00:04:00,546 --> 00:04:06,609
$45,990 drive-away, rising
to $46,990 after the

71
00:04:06,659 --> 00:04:09,129
30th of November 2026.

72
00:04:09,179 --> 00:04:12,069
The H7 Lux plug-in hybrid:

73
00:04:12,119 --> 00:04:18,349
$49,990 drive-away, rising
to $50,990 after the 30th

74
00:04:18,399 --> 00:04:18,829
of November.

75
00:04:18,879 --> 00:04:24,209
The higher-spec Vanta
hybrid: $49,990 drive-away.

76
00:04:24,259 --> 00:04:27,919
And the Vanta plug-in
hybrid: $53,990 drive-away.

77
00:04:27,969 --> 00:04:33,969
The Lux gets 19-inch wheels, a 15.6-inch
touchscreen and a head-up display.

78
00:04:34,019 --> 00:04:36,089
The Vanta adds a locking
rear differential,

79
00:04:36,139 --> 00:04:40,429
a panoramic sunroof, heated and ventilated
front seats and ambient lighting.

80
00:04:40,479 --> 00:04:43,149
A seven-seat version is due in 2027.

81
00:04:43,199 --> 00:04:46,409
And GWM has been sharpening
prices across its whole range.

82
00:04:46,459 --> 00:04:48,449
In October 2026,

83
00:04:48,499 --> 00:04:53,529
CarsGuide reported the Haval Jolion
Premium at $23,990 drive-away,

84
00:04:53,579 --> 00:05:00,089
$3,000 off, and the Haval
H6 hybrid Lux at $37,990,

85
00:05:00,139 --> 00:05:02,089
also $3,000 off.

86
00:05:02,139 --> 00:05:05,209
So the H7's launch pricing
fits a clear strategy:

87
00:05:05,259 --> 00:05:09,029
lots of car for the money, with
the price including on-road costs.

88
00:05:09,079 --> 00:05:10,509
Now, one important detail.

89
00:05:10,559 --> 00:05:12,789
Those H7 prices are drive-away.

90
00:05:12,839 --> 00:05:15,819
Most Toyota prices are
quoted before on-road costs.

91
00:05:15,869 --> 00:05:18,749
On-road costs things like stamp duty,

92
00:05:18,799 --> 00:05:22,009
registration and CTP insurance
can add thousands of dollars,

93
00:05:22,059 --> 00:05:23,749
depending on your state.

94
00:05:23,799 --> 00:05:27,529
So when you compare the two, you have
to compare drive-away with drive-away.

95
00:05:27,579 --> 00:05:30,119
Otherwise, the gap looks
smaller than it really is.

96
00:05:30,855 --> 00:05:32,465
Now let's look at the champion.

97
00:05:32,515 --> 00:05:35,925
The Toyota RAV4 is one of the
best-selling cars in Australia.

98
00:05:35,975 --> 00:05:40,765
And when Toyota added its first-ever
RAV4 plug-in hybrid in mid-2026,

99
00:05:40,815 --> 00:05:41,865
it took off.

100
00:05:41,915 --> 00:05:43,058
According to CarExpert,

101
00:05:43,108 --> 00:05:48,685
plug-in hybrids made up thirty-nine
per cent of all RAV4 sales in July 2026

102
00:05:48,735 --> 00:05:51,185
around 2,170 cars.

103
00:05:51,235 --> 00:05:55,345
That made the RAV4 PHEV the best-selling
plug-in hybrid in the country that

104
00:05:55,395 --> 00:05:57,505
month, ahead of the BYD Shark 6.

105
00:05:57,555 --> 00:06:01,985
Here's the current RAV4 plug-in
hybrid range, before on-road costs.

106
00:06:02,035 --> 00:06:06,605
The XSE front-wheel
drive starts at $58,840.

107
00:06:06,655 --> 00:06:11,345
The XSE all-wheel drive is $63,340.

108
00:06:11,395 --> 00:06:16,085
And the GR Sport all-wheel
drive is $66,340.

109
00:06:16,135 --> 00:06:19,425
It uses a 2.5-litre petrol
engine with electric motors,

110
00:06:19,475 --> 00:06:23,105
producing 201 kilowatts
in front-wheel drive form,

111
00:06:23,155 --> 00:06:26,625
and Toyota claims an electric-only
range of 121 kilometres.

112
00:06:26,675 --> 00:06:28,845
And the regular RAV4 hybrid?

113
00:06:28,895 --> 00:06:34,985
CarExpert listed the RAV4 GX
two-wheel-drive hybrid from $45,990

114
00:06:35,035 --> 00:06:36,705
before on-road costs.

115
00:06:36,755 --> 00:06:43,025
So the H7 Lux hybrid's launch price of
$45,990 drive-away matches the cheapest

116
00:06:43,075 --> 00:06:47,655
RAV4 hybrid's sticker price but includes
on-road costs and all-wheel drive.

117
00:06:48,443 --> 00:06:49,863
Let's put them side by side.

118
00:06:49,913 --> 00:06:52,393
Plug-in hybrid versus plug-in hybrid.

119
00:06:52,443 --> 00:06:54,753
The H7 Lux PHEV:

120
00:06:54,803 --> 00:06:58,913
$49,990 drive-away, 320 kilowatts,

121
00:06:58,963 --> 00:07:03,473
all-wheel drive, 137 kilometres
of claimed electric range.

122
00:07:03,523 --> 00:07:07,273
The RAV4 XSE PHEV front-wheel drive:

123
00:07:07,323 --> 00:07:10,440
$58,840 before on-road costs,

124
00:07:10,490 --> 00:07:14,573
201 kilowatts, 121 kilometres
of claimed electric range.

125
00:07:14,623 --> 00:07:15,833
On those numbers,

126
00:07:15,883 --> 00:07:20,163
the GWM is around nine thousand dollars
cheaper before you even add the RAV4's

127
00:07:20,213 --> 00:07:21,553
on-road costs.

128
00:07:21,603 --> 00:07:22,933
It's much more powerful.

129
00:07:22,983 --> 00:07:24,793
And it claims more electric range.

130
00:07:24,843 --> 00:07:28,513
The H7's electric range figure
is on the Chinese WLTC cycle,

131
00:07:28,563 --> 00:07:32,173
though, so it's not a perfect
like-for-like comparison with every rival.

132
00:07:32,223 --> 00:07:35,473
Real-world range will depend
on how and where you drive.

133
00:07:35,523 --> 00:07:39,813
On features, the H7 Lux also comes
with a lot as standard for the price,

134
00:07:39,863 --> 00:07:43,473
including that 15.6-inch
touchscreen and a head-up display.

135
00:07:43,523 --> 00:07:45,413
When you compare the two in a showroom,

136
00:07:45,463 --> 00:07:49,033
make a list of what you actually need
and check which features are standard on

137
00:07:49,083 --> 00:07:52,793
the exact grade you're looking at, not
just the top model in the brochure.

138
00:07:52,843 --> 00:07:54,600
And for families who
mostly do short trips,

139
00:07:54,650 --> 00:07:58,973
a claimed 137 kilometres of
electric range is a big deal.

140
00:07:59,023 --> 00:08:00,553
If you charge at home every night,

141
00:08:00,603 --> 00:08:04,293
many commutes and school runs could be
done without burning any petrol at all.

142
00:08:04,343 --> 00:08:06,993
Let's do a quick illustration
and I want to be clear,

143
00:08:07,043 --> 00:08:09,073
these are example numbers,
not official figures.

144
00:08:09,123 --> 00:08:13,973
Say you drive forty kilometres a
day, about 14,600 kilometres a year.

145
00:08:14,023 --> 00:08:16,633
A petrol SUV using seven
litres per hundred kilometres,

146
00:08:16,683 --> 00:08:21,733
at two dollars a litre, would
cost around $2,044 a year in fuel.

147
00:08:21,783 --> 00:08:24,993
If you could do most of that driving
on electricity charged at home,

148
00:08:25,043 --> 00:08:27,966
and your plug-in hybrid used around
twenty kilowatt-hours per hundred

149
00:08:28,016 --> 00:08:33,413
kilometres at thirty cents per
kilowatt-hour, that's around $876 a year.

150
00:08:33,463 --> 00:08:35,873
Your own numbers will depend
on your electricity plan,

151
00:08:35,923 --> 00:08:37,133
your driving and the car.

152
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:41,313
But it shows why electric range
matters so much for daily drivers.

153
00:08:41,363 --> 00:08:43,473
But there are things the
brochure doesn't tell you.

154
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:44,963
And that's where it gets interesting.

155
00:08:45,827 --> 00:08:47,637
Quick favour before we go deeper.

156
00:08:47,687 --> 00:08:49,297
Which would you buy the cheaper,

157
00:08:49,347 --> 00:08:53,297
more powerful GWM, or the Toyota
with the badge and the reputation?

158
00:08:53,347 --> 00:08:54,537
Tell me in the comments.

159
00:08:54,587 --> 00:08:55,437
And if you want honest,

160
00:08:55,487 --> 00:08:59,497
fact-checked comparisons of the cars
Aussies actually buy, hit subscribe.

161
00:08:59,547 --> 00:09:01,707
It's free and it really helps the channel.

162
00:09:03,609 --> 00:09:03,612
First, towing.

163
00:09:03,662 --> 00:09:05,272
Australians love to tow.

164
00:09:05,322 --> 00:09:10,132
CarExpert lists the new H7's braked
towing capacity at 1,500 kilograms,

165
00:09:10,182 --> 00:09:13,132
for both the hybrid
and the plug-in hybrid.

166
00:09:13,182 --> 00:09:15,812
That's fine for a small
trailer or a light camper.

167
00:09:15,862 --> 00:09:18,672
But if you're planning to tow
a large caravan or a boat,

168
00:09:18,722 --> 00:09:22,692
check the exact towing figures for every
car you're considering before you buy

169
00:09:22,742 --> 00:09:26,492
and remember that plug-in hybrids use
more fuel and electricity when towing.

170
00:09:26,542 --> 00:09:28,712
Second, warranty.

171
00:09:28,762 --> 00:09:30,599
GWM offers a seven-year,

172
00:09:30,649 --> 00:09:32,632
unlimited-kilometre
warranty on its vehicles,

173
00:09:32,682 --> 00:09:34,692
according to its Australian website.

174
00:09:34,742 --> 00:09:38,072
And its hybrid and plug-in hybrid
batteries are covered for eight years with

175
00:09:38,122 --> 00:09:39,632
unlimited kilometres.

176
00:09:39,682 --> 00:09:41,352
One detail in the fine print:

177
00:09:41,402 --> 00:09:43,532
for plug-in hybrids and EVs,

178
00:09:43,582 --> 00:09:47,532
GWM says a battery state of health
of seventy per cent or more isn't

179
00:09:47,582 --> 00:09:49,652
considered a warranty defect.

180
00:09:49,702 --> 00:09:53,099
Toyota's base warranty is five
years with unlimited kilometres.

181
00:09:53,149 --> 00:09:57,432
CarsGuide reported that Toyota extends
engine and driveline cover to up to

182
00:09:57,482 --> 00:10:00,772
seven years, and hybrid battery
cover to up to ten years,

183
00:10:00,822 --> 00:10:03,992
as long as the car is serviced and
maintained according to the warranty and

184
00:10:04,042 --> 00:10:05,012
service book.

185
00:10:05,062 --> 00:10:05,872
So on paper,

186
00:10:05,922 --> 00:10:08,692
the warranties are closer than they
first look but the conditions are

187
00:10:08,742 --> 00:10:10,782
different, and it's
worth reading them both.

188
00:10:11,596 --> 00:10:14,766
And one more thing for anyone
thinking about salary packaging.

189
00:10:14,816 --> 00:10:18,346
Neither of these cars gets the fringe
benefits tax exemption on a novated

190
00:10:18,396 --> 00:10:18,956
lease.

191
00:10:19,006 --> 00:10:23,406
Plug-in hybrids lost that
exemption on the 1st of April 2025.

192
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:25,926
Only fully electric cars still qualify.

193
00:10:25,976 --> 00:10:27,986
So if you're comparing
these two through a lease,

194
00:10:28,036 --> 00:10:31,706
the tax treatment is the same but if
you're also considering a fully electric

195
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:34,626
SUV, that could change the maths a lot.

196
00:10:34,676 --> 00:10:37,586
Third, and this is the
big one: resale value.

197
00:10:37,636 --> 00:10:39,926
Toyota's reputation for
holding value is famous.

198
00:10:39,976 --> 00:10:45,166
A 2025 analysis by Pickles and Datium
Insights found that a two-year-old

199
00:10:45,216 --> 00:10:48,886
Toyota RAV4 kept about
eighty-eight per cent of its value.

200
00:10:48,936 --> 00:10:51,826
That's one of the best results
of any car in Australia.

201
00:10:51,876 --> 00:10:56,226
We don't yet have long-term resale
data for the new H7 it's brand new.

202
00:10:56,276 --> 00:10:58,066
But the broader story is clear:

203
00:10:58,116 --> 00:11:02,366
newer brands, and models that get
replaced quickly, often lose value faster.

204
00:11:02,416 --> 00:11:05,386
The old H7 was replaced
after just over a year.

205
00:11:05,436 --> 00:11:08,206
And when a model gets a quick
facelift or a big price cut,

206
00:11:08,256 --> 00:11:11,346
the value of the older
version usually takes a hit.

207
00:11:11,396 --> 00:11:15,366
One Cars24 reader put it bluntly
in the comments on the H7's launch:

208
00:11:15,416 --> 00:11:19,386
there's "no promotional discount for a
car delivered in Nov/Dec," and it "will

209
00:11:19,436 --> 00:11:24,366
lose value as soon as we hit 2027."
That's one buyer's opinion, not data.

210
00:11:24,416 --> 00:11:26,166
But it's a fair point to think about.

211
00:11:26,216 --> 00:11:28,626
If you buy any car in
November or December,

212
00:11:28,676 --> 00:11:31,806
it'll be a year older on
paper just weeks later.

213
00:11:31,856 --> 00:11:33,186
Insurance is worth checking too.

214
00:11:33,236 --> 00:11:35,546
In April 2026,

215
00:11:35,596 --> 00:11:38,566
Compare the Market reported that
average premiums for battery electric

216
00:11:38,616 --> 00:11:41,346
vehicles had risen about
ten per cent in a year,

217
00:11:41,396 --> 00:11:45,766
and that average premiums for some
plug-in hybrids like the BYD Sealion 6 had

218
00:11:45,816 --> 00:11:47,526
risen about eighteen per cent.

219
00:11:47,576 --> 00:11:50,086
Premiums vary a lot by insurer, model,

220
00:11:50,136 --> 00:11:54,326
postcode and driver, so get real
quotes for both cars before you decide.

221
00:11:54,376 --> 00:11:57,426
So when you compare the two, don't
just look at the price you pay.

222
00:11:57,476 --> 00:11:59,226
Look at the price you'll
get back when you sell.

223
00:11:59,276 --> 00:12:03,146
A car that's nine thousand dollars cheaper
but loses ten thousand dollars more

224
00:12:03,196 --> 00:12:05,216
in value isn't actually cheaper.

225
00:12:06,025 --> 00:12:07,975
Before we get to Toyota's counter-attack,

226
00:12:08,025 --> 00:12:11,755
there's one more thing worth considering:
the dealer and service network.

227
00:12:11,805 --> 00:12:14,675
Toyota has one of the largest
dealer networks in Australia,

228
00:12:14,725 --> 00:12:16,315
including in regional towns.

229
00:12:16,365 --> 00:12:20,115
That matters for servicing,
warranty repairs and crash repairs.

230
00:12:20,165 --> 00:12:23,015
As we saw in our video
on BYD after the crash,

231
00:12:23,065 --> 00:12:26,575
a great car can still be a frustrating
ownership experience if parts take

232
00:12:26,625 --> 00:12:29,875
weeks or the nearest approved
repairer is hours away.

233
00:12:29,925 --> 00:12:34,035
GWM has been in Australia for eighteen
years and has a substantial network,

234
00:12:34,085 --> 00:12:35,675
but before you buy any car,

235
00:12:35,725 --> 00:12:39,375
check where your nearest service centre
and approved repairer actually are.

236
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:42,375
And here's the twist:
Toyota isn't standing still.

237
00:12:42,425 --> 00:12:44,775
In the first three months of 2027,

238
00:12:44,825 --> 00:12:48,175
Toyota is adding a cheaper
RAV4 GXL plug-in hybrid.

239
00:12:48,225 --> 00:12:50,055
Toyota hasn't announced the price yet.

240
00:12:50,105 --> 00:12:55,955
CarExpert estimated it could be
around $53,990 before on-road costs,

241
00:12:56,005 --> 00:13:00,015
based on the gap between the hybrid and
plug-in hybrid versions of the RAV4.

242
00:13:00,065 --> 00:13:01,895
That's an estimate,
not an official figure.

243
00:13:01,945 --> 00:13:06,375
It's expected to use the same
201-kilowatt plug-in hybrid system with a

244
00:13:06,425 --> 00:13:09,535
claimed 121 kilometres of electric range,

245
00:13:09,585 --> 00:13:12,475
and to become the most
affordable RAV4 plug-in hybrid.

246
00:13:12,525 --> 00:13:16,915
CarExpert also said it's expected to
undercut the Mitsubishi Outlander plug-in

247
00:13:16,965 --> 00:13:22,675
hybrid, which starts at
$58,990 before on-road costs.

248
00:13:22,725 --> 00:13:24,615
Why is Toyota moving so fast?

249
00:13:24,665 --> 00:13:26,455
Partly because of the
government's emissions rules.

250
00:13:26,505 --> 00:13:29,135
Under the New Vehicle Efficiency Standard,

251
00:13:29,185 --> 00:13:33,595
the target for passenger cars drops
from 117 grams of carbon dioxide per

252
00:13:33,645 --> 00:13:37,635
kilometre in 2026 to 92 grams in 2027.

253
00:13:37,685 --> 00:13:41,455
Plug-in hybrids help car
makers hit those targets.

254
00:13:41,505 --> 00:13:44,995
Toyota is already earning credits
thanks to its hybrids but it needs them,

255
00:13:45,045 --> 00:13:48,795
because its utes and big four-wheel
drives are well above the targets.

256
00:13:48,845 --> 00:13:52,435
Every RAV4 plug-in hybrid it
sells helps balance the books.

257
00:13:52,485 --> 00:13:53,975
So in 2027,

258
00:13:54,025 --> 00:13:59,375
the gap between the RAV4 PHEV and the
H7 PHEV could shrink although if that

259
00:13:59,425 --> 00:14:00,335
estimate is right,

260
00:14:00,385 --> 00:14:04,535
the RAV4 would still be more expensive
once on-road costs are added.

261
00:14:04,585 --> 00:14:06,395
GWM is moving too.

262
00:14:06,445 --> 00:14:09,395
The seven-seat H7, due in 2027,

263
00:14:09,445 --> 00:14:15,435
gets a longer 2,850-millimetre wheelbase
and stretches to 4,912 millimetres

264
00:14:15,485 --> 00:14:16,055
long.

265
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:19,955
That puts it into the territory of
bigger family SUVs a part of the market

266
00:14:20,005 --> 00:14:22,195
where Toyota doesn't sell a RAV4 at all.

267
00:14:22,245 --> 00:14:26,115
And GWM won't be the only
one fighting for RAV4 buyers.

268
00:14:26,165 --> 00:14:30,545
The plug-in hybrid SUV market is
packed with Chinese rivals from BYD,

269
00:14:30,595 --> 00:14:34,535
Chery, Geely and Omoda Jaecoo
many of them with big batteries,

270
00:14:34,585 --> 00:14:37,235
lots of equipment and
sharp drive-away prices.

271
00:14:37,285 --> 00:14:41,735
In September 2026, BYD was
Australia's second best-selling brand.

272
00:14:41,785 --> 00:14:43,585
The pressure on Toyota is real.

273
00:14:44,380 --> 00:14:46,130
So, which one should you buy?

274
00:14:46,180 --> 00:14:47,650
Here's how I'd decide.

275
00:14:47,700 --> 00:14:51,610
Buy the GWM Haval H7
plug-in hybrid if price,

276
00:14:51,660 --> 00:14:54,270
power and electric range
matter most to you.

277
00:14:54,320 --> 00:14:55,870
If you do lots of short trips,

278
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:59,210
can charge at home, want all-wheel
drive and a long warranty,

279
00:14:59,260 --> 00:15:03,830
and plan to keep the car for a long
time so resale value matters less the H7

280
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:05,770
offers a lot of car for the money.

281
00:15:05,820 --> 00:15:09,310
Buy the Toyota RAV4 plug-in
hybrid if resale value,

282
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:11,770
brand reputation and
dealer network matter most.

283
00:15:11,820 --> 00:15:15,650
Toyota's history of holding value
and its huge service network,

284
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:18,770
especially in regional
Australia, are real advantages.

285
00:15:18,820 --> 00:15:21,330
And if you can wait until early 2027,

286
00:15:21,380 --> 00:15:24,810
the cheaper GXL plug-in hybrid
could narrow the price gap.

287
00:15:24,860 --> 00:15:27,310
And think about how you'll
actually use the battery.

288
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:30,850
A plug-in hybrid only saves you
real money if you plug it in.

289
00:15:30,900 --> 00:15:32,250
If you can't charge at home,

290
00:15:32,300 --> 00:15:34,390
or you mostly do long highway trips,

291
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:39,970
a regular hybrid like the H7 hybrid or
the RAV4 hybrid may make more sense,

292
00:15:40,020 --> 00:15:40,870
and it's cheaper to buy.

293
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:46,210
With petrol and diesel prices as volatile
as they've been in 2026 diesel hit

294
00:15:46,260 --> 00:15:50,170
as high as $3.50 a litre in
some parts of Australia in May,

295
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:53,650
according to CarExpert the right
choice depends on your driving,

296
00:15:53,700 --> 00:15:54,590
not the brochure.

297
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:57,350
On the test drive, pay
attention to a few things.

298
00:15:57,400 --> 00:16:00,690
How does the car drive when the battery
is flat and the petrol engine is doing

299
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:01,490
the work?

300
00:16:01,540 --> 00:16:02,850
Is the engine noisy?

301
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:06,430
How easy are the touchscreen and the
driver assistance systems to live with?

302
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:09,610
And how much boot space is left
once the charging cable is in there?

303
00:16:09,660 --> 00:16:13,430
These are the things that make a car
pleasant or annoying after the first

304
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:14,450
week.

305
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:17,210
And whichever you choose,
do these four things.

306
00:16:17,260 --> 00:16:18,350
Test drive both.

307
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:21,310
Compare drive-away prices,
not sticker prices.

308
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:23,390
Check towing capacity if you tow.

309
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,370
And look at the real running costs:

310
00:16:25,420 --> 00:16:28,480
fuel, electricity,
servicing and insurance.

311
00:16:29,479 --> 00:16:32,309
One last tip if you're
buying in the next few weeks.

312
00:16:32,359 --> 00:16:37,029
The H7 Lux launch prices go up by a
thousand dollars after the 30th of

313
00:16:37,079 --> 00:16:38,489
November 2026.

314
00:16:38,539 --> 00:16:41,389
And Black Friday is on
the 27th of November.

315
00:16:41,439 --> 00:16:44,149
If you've decided on the
H7, that's your window.

316
00:16:44,199 --> 00:16:46,469
But as we covered in
our Black Friday video,

317
00:16:46,519 --> 00:16:48,549
write down today's drive-away price,

318
00:16:48,599 --> 00:16:51,669
